                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Magicat especially for the price really and I do mean REALLY! Caught me off guard, here we have a cute sidescrolling platformer game that has it's fair share of challenges, special items you can buy for playing good that provide permanent and extremely handy (mostly) effects and a lot of level variety, this is a game that is frankly begging people to buy it not out of desperation to sell well, in my eyes it's earned that, it wants to get out there and let players enjoy and it really is just enjoyable and creative and weird for reasons you will see if ya buy it dood. XD\r\n\r\nAlright full review time! Magicat Starts you off as a cat! Of who is magical! Who could have guessed that? *wink wink* something was stolen and as the guardinyan? Of this object you now adventure furth to retrieve it from the thief dood!\r\n\r\nThe game plays basically but expands a little, you start with a jump, a dash, you can duck, crawl while doing so and most importantly you barf out magic furballs! Well okay you shoot magic out your mouth but I think of them as lethal furballs at least dood.\r\n\r\nEach stage has three areas with three collectables of which to purchase special upgrades in stores scattered around the map and a boss at the end of those three areas, you get checkpoints that cost you 10 (hecking lots) of mana to use in each area, magic is used for your dash so that's a steep price but for a handy function, that said if you die you can spend paw currency! This is used for certain...map functions I'll say but in game every time you die you can spend some to revive there and then! It gets more expensive each time but unless you're really terrible at the game you shouldn't need too many dood (I ended on like 2300ish, cat's got way more than 9 lives!!)\r\n\r\nThe map is interesting, you have multiple paths to go down and multiple stages in turn to go through, with the right items you can do a couple of interesting things on the map, even straight up skip stages up until the end even if you wanna skip it all for some crazy reason, maybe speed running if that's your thing, there's even hidden treasures out there that will come in handy for getting more items from the shop, sweet deal dood!\r\n\r\nThe story is...uhhh interesting? XD It's a lot of meows and various animal noises (in writing) and you having to work it out yourself, which it's easy enough to do but like what world is this!? The music is pretty nice too, it certainly had a couple I really enjoyed playing to dood.\r\n\r\nThe difficulty varies on a lot of things you do, I'd say only one boss was truly difficult, like it almost got me good level of hard XD and the puzzles for getting the three collectable items in stages will likely kill you before anything else in the game does unless you're rushing, you also have a timer mode you can do, I appreciate highly that you skip the bosses at the end for it XD really for achievements and extra paw currency though dood.\r\n\r\nAnd that's about it really, issues with the game? Well I'd say one is a bug, playing on steam machine granted but eventually I find the frames start skipping and it makes playing a little more awkward, easy fix though, just quit and start it back up again so nothing game breaking, some puzzles despite giving you everything you need can be a little too brutal on time they give you or conditions but that said you don't need them all for anything but achievements so it's also not a deal breaker, honestly this is a dang solid game that especially right now as I wright this (it's on offer the £0.85/$0.99) is on a stellar offer, you just can't go wrong dood! \r\n\r\nThank you for reading! I hope you enjoy the game as much as I did if you buy it dood! ^-^7",
